The habit that AI researchers have of pretending that disagreeing with their sexual norms is the same as committing a crime is deeply immoral and actively undermines actual safety.

@AdrianTMiranda notes that a preprint from about a year ago discussed how abliteration has become much easier since then. The field itself hosts abliterated models that can be used maliciously.

The linked paper, arXiv:2508.12622, explores how uncensored large language models are used in cybercrimes, highlighting the risks associated with such models.

Nothing useful will come from this, because what really matters is corporate decision-making at OpenAI and why they keep making insane decisions. I have low expectations for the technical analysis, but I also think it doesn’t matter.

Questions I would like to know the answer to…

